; example.com.'s own authoritative zone: A/AAAA at the apex, a CNAME, an MX,
; a TXT record, and a further delegation down to "dev.example.com." (its own
; server, its own glue) to demonstrate a second level of real delegation.
$TTL 3600
$ORIGIN example.com.
@                        IN  SOA  ns1.example.com. hostmaster.example.com. (
                                  2026081401
                                  3600
                                  900
                                  604800
                                  3600 )
@                        IN  NS    ns1.example.com.
ns1.example.com.         IN  A     127.0.0.4
@                        IN  A     93.184.216.34
@                        IN  AAAA  2606:2800:220:1:248:1893:25c8:1946
@                        IN  MX    10 mail.example.com.
@                        IN  TXT   "v=spf1 -all"
www                      IN  CNAME @
mail                     IN  A     93.184.216.40

dev.example.com.         IN  NS    ns1.dev.example.com.
ns1.dev.example.com.     IN  A     127.0.0.5
